from pathlib import Path
ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
BLOCK = "### Native-source scalar representation and State runtime\n\nNative-source Email/Business/Provider/Configs/Skill/Sync and State storage encode finite REAL values as an exact binary significand and exponent and decode them with SQLite's built-in pow, preserving native TEXT/INTEGER affinity results. Scalar binding reads float and string subclasses through their base implementations and bytes through the buffer protocol, matching sqlite3's underlying bound value. Non-C-contiguous buffers retain native BufferError behavior. The shared encoder validates the underlying integer against SQLite's signed 64-bit range before serialization. Published Reply retains its existing scalar format; frozen source fingerprints remain unchanged.\n\nStore20/Email52 uses one State table for fifteen retained native state kinds. Fresh Store-first and Email-first construction creates this declaration; current callers use the existing State projections and transaction-owned write primitives. The paired release retires sixteen native State tables, including the eligible empty corpus source table. Original unused conversation fields are retired only when their existing source eligibility check permits it. Archived native factories and historical release source contracts remain unchanged.\n\nState INSERT, point UPDATE, UPSERT and bulk UPDATE keep caller-owned transactions and do not commit or roll back earlier caller work. Omitted defaults and OR REPLACE substitutions for supplied NULL/NaN on defaulted NOT NULL fields execute inside the final write statement. Nullable NULL and defaultless NOT NULL failures retain native behavior. Bulk updates preserve one-statement affected-row counts, ABORT behavior, original-row expressions and untouched encoded leaves. SQLite CURRENT_TIMESTAMP remains statement-stable.\n\nState UPSERT uses the existing source-key partial unique index in one INSERT. Original INSERT-candidate constraints run before a conflict update, including explicit NULL on a required wizard confirmer, even when an update guard is false. Matched rows keep their source identity and change only selected payload leaves. No failed SQL operation retries a different storage layout.\n\nOrganization name and open DingTalk ID indexes use the original source ROWID as the final key, preserving equal-key encounter order independently of State physical IDs. Current declaration checking sorts index records by name and omits only SQLite's index enumeration seq; SQL, ordered columns, uniqueness, origin, partial predicates, foreign keys and triggers remain exact. Source declarations and physical State DDL are unchanged. Current constructors retain only the existing two dispatcher-index repairs and reject unsupported namespace collisions before changing journal mode or DDL.\n\nCurrent session, conversation, lock, route, wizard, scan/history cursor, reaction, health and deferral callers use State. Dispatcher ownership, generation, terminal/expiry predicates, cancellation fences and task eligibility retain their existing business rules. Empty dispatcher probes remain read-only; positive claims recheck inside the existing writer transaction.\n\nPublication readers choose the native historical source or exact current State marker explicitly. A malformed current declaration never retries native. The seven generic current publication selectors require the complete current Actions/Skill receipt declaration; Email availability and action publication retain their existing Store/Email marker-pair contract. Store-only current databases do not advertise an Email runtime.\n\nPaired forward migration captures State declarations only, converts State after Configs and writes the Store marker and Email ledger with the same existing timestamp in the original atomic transaction. Target verification reads the current State marker. Inverse restores State first from current facts, then preserves the existing Configs/Business/Email/Provider inverse sequence and original native marker/ledger restoration. It does not restore State rows from an earlier snapshot.\n\nUpgrade progress selects the committed schema at DAO construction and immediately before native DAO progress writes. One read-only snapshot observes the retained Email ledger first: positive native versions through source51 select native service_state and target52 selects State; malformed or unsupported future ledger versions remain visible errors. Without a ledger version, Store-only State requires its exact current Store marker; missing paths and empty databases remain source without creating files or tables. Explicit getters/setters keep their original transactions and bounded lock/busy retry and do not reselect after SQL failure. Generic protocol stores are unchanged. Progress after a child commit or inverse follows the actual committed role, including a commit that becomes durable before an exception is reported.\n"
for name in ("docs/architecture.md", "docs/runtime-mechanism.md"):
    path = ROOT / name
    text = path.read_text()
    start = text.index("### Exact native-source scalar representation (unpublished)")
    if name.endswith("architecture.md"):
        last = "For `OR REPLACE` point writes,"
    else:
        last = "The upgrade progress DAO starts explicitly bound"
    final_start = text.index(last, start)
    end = text.index("\n", final_start)
    text = text[:start] + BLOCK.rstrip() + "\n" + text[end:]
    # The explicit selector option is now used by the current readers.
    text = text.replace(
        "Current State callers and publication remain unselected.",
        "Current State Memory and generic publication readers explicitly select this option.",
    )
    text = text.replace(
        "Current State callers and publication remain unselected; this change does not publish a deployment.",
        "Current State Memory and generic publication readers explicitly select this option; deployment remains separate.",
    )
    text = text.replace("current callers and schema publication/release remain unselected.",
                        "current State Memory and generic publication readers select the complete current declaration.")
    path.write_text(text)
